{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdlib>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\nconst ll MOD = 1000000007LL;\nconst int MAXN = 1000007;\nll P, K;\nll mark[MAXN];\nll count_arr[MAXN];\n\nll fast_pow(ll base, ll exp) {\n    ll result = 1;\n    base %= MOD;\n    while (exp) {\n        if (exp & 1) result = (result * base) % MOD;\n        base = (base * base) % MOD;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nll helper(int len) {\n    ll base = (count_arr[len] * len) % MOD;\n    base = (base + 1) % MOD;\n    return fast_pow(base, count_arr[len]);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    cin >> P >> K;\n    for (int i = 0; i < MAXN; i++) {\n        mark[i] = 0;\n        count_arr[i] = 0;\n    }\n    if (K == 0) {\n        cout << fast_pow(P, P - 1) << \"\\n\";\n        return 0;\n    }\n    if (K == 1) {\n        cout << fast_pow(P, P) << \"\\n\";\n        return 0;\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < P; i++) {\n        if (!mark[i]) {\n            ll len = 0;\n            ll pos = i;\n            while (!mark[pos]) {\n                mark[pos] = 1;\n                len++;\n                pos = (K * pos) % P;\n            }\n            count_arr[len]++;\n        }\n    }\n    ll ans = 1;\n    for (int i = 2; i < P; i++) {\n        if (count_arr[i]) {\n            ans = (ans * helper(i)) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << ans << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef fast_pow(base, exp):\n    return pow(base, exp, MOD)\n\ndef helper(length, count):\n    base = (count * length) % MOD\n    base = (base + 1) % MOD\n    return fast_pow(base, count)\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    P = int(data[0])\n    K = int(data[1])\n    \n    if K == 0:\n        print(fast_pow(P, P - 1))\n        return\n    if K == 1:\n        print(fast_pow(P, P))\n        return\n    \n    mark = [0] * P\n    count_arr = [0] * (P + 1)  # index up to P\n    \n    for i in range(P):\n        if not mark[i]:\n            length = 0\n            pos = i\n            while not mark[pos]:\n                mark[pos] = 1\n                length += 1\n                pos = (K * pos) % P\n            count_arr[length] += 1\n    \n    ans = 1\n    for i in range(2, P):\n        if count_arr[i]:\n            ans = (ans * helper(i, count_arr[i])) % MOD\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.125868119648658e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00018726025882642716, -0.16994400322437286, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.005238852929323912, -0.005234820768237114, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.7205765440594405e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.008637331426143646, -2.002696055569686e-05, -0.22093641757965088, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -2.861018856492592e-06, -0.014163801446557045, -3.099436753473128e-06, -0.0